<h2 id="bottom-line">Bottom Line</h2>

<p>The Kindle Scribe Colorsoft is the clearest example yet of where e-readers are heading: bigger screens, color e-ink, and handwriting as a first-class feature. TechCrunch's two-month test confirms it is a genuinely excellent tool for the reader who annotates — and a genuinely poor value for everyone else at $630.</p>

<p>If that describes your reading life, the device earns its price: color-coded highlights on your EPUBs, a reading journal that never leaves your hands, and battery life measured in weeks. If it does not, the smart money is on the Paperwhite today and on the Kobo path if you want native EPUB freedom. Either way, the EPUB library you build with Calibre and DRM-free files will be ready for whichever device wins your desk.</p>
